!script {{
  --/| ==========================================================================
  --/| Tutorial: Arrays and Hashtables from Beacon Repeating Rows
  --/|
  --/| PURPOSE
  --/| The repeating-row tutorials showed how to load and read one row at a time.
  --/| Sometimes a script needs the whole section in a form that is easier to
  --/| work with later.
  --/|
  --/| ScriptCards can turn repeating-row information into an array or hashtable.
  --/|
  --/| An ARRAY is simply an ordered list of values.
  --/| Example: Bite, Claw, Multiattack
  --/|
  --/| A HASHTABLE is a collection of named values. Instead of remembering a
  --/| position, the script looks up information using a key.
  --/|
  --/| HOW TO USE IT
  --/| 1. Select a D&D 2024 Beacon NPC with at least one normal Action.
  --/| 2. Run this ScriptCard.
  --/| 3. The tutorial converts repeating_npcaction into several useful forms.
  --/|
  --/| WHAT THIS TEACHES
  --/| array;fromrepeatingsection collects one field from every repeating row.
  --/| In this tutorial it collects the name from every Action.
  --/|
  --/| array;fullrepeatingsection can combine several fields from each row into
  --/| one array entry.
  --/|
  --/| hashtable;fromrepeatingsection builds keys using an identifier field.
  --/| The identifier values should be unique. For an Action section, name is
  --/| convenient when every action has a different name.
  --/|
  --/| hashtable;fromrepeatingrow builds a small hashtable for just one row.
  --/|
  --/| The identifier field used by hashtable;fromrepeatingsection must be written
  --/| in lower case.
  --/|
  --/| This tutorial only reads information. It does not change the character.
  --/| ==========================================================================

  --#beaconsheet|1
  --#sourcetoken|@{selected|token_id}
  --#title|[*S:character_name] - Arrays and Hashtables Tutorial

  --&CharacterID|[*S:character_id]
  --&Section|repeating_npcaction
  --&RowCount|[*R:[&CharacterID]:[&Section]:rowcount]

  --+|[c][b]Section Overview[/b][/c]

  --+Section|[&Section]
  --+Number of Rows|[&RowCount]

  --?"[&RowCount]" -eq "0"|NoRows

  --+|[c][b]Create an Array of Action Names[/b][/c]

  --/| This collects the name field from every row into ActionNames.
  --~|array;fromrepeatingsection;ActionNames;[&CharacterID];[&Section];name

  --+Array Length|[@ActionNames()]
  --+First Array Entry|[@ActionNames(0)]

  --/| foreach runs the following lines once for every value in the array.
  --%ActionName|foreach;ActionNames
    --+Action Name|[&ActionName]
  --%|

  --+|[c][b]Create a Full-Row Array[/b][/c]

  --/| This combines each row's name and row ID, separated by a tilde.
  --~|array;fullrepeatingsection;FullActions;[&CharacterID];[&Section];name:xxxActionIDxxxx;~

  --+Full Array Length|[@FullActions()]
  --+First Combined Entry|[@FullActions(0)]

  --+|[c][b]Create a Hashtable from the Whole Section[/b][/c]

  --/| Here name is the identifier. A key is built from the action name plus the
  --/| field we want. For example: Bite_description or Bite_sectionid.
  --~|hashtable;fromrepeatingsection;[&CharacterID];[&Section];name;ActionHash

  --/| Save the first action name so we can use it as part of a hashtable key.
  --&FirstActionName|[@ActionNames(0)]

  --+First Action|[&FirstActionName]
  --+Description from Hash|[:ActionHash("[&FirstActionName]_description")]
  --+Row ID from Hash|[:ActionHash("[&FirstActionName]_sectionid")]

  --+|[c][b]Create a Hashtable from One Row[/b][/c]

  --/| First save the row ID from the section hashtable.
  --&FirstActionID|[:ActionHash("[&FirstActionName]_sectionid")]

  --/| Now build a hashtable containing only that one repeating row.
  --~|hashtable;fromrepeatingrow;[&CharacterID];[&Section];[&FirstActionID];OneAction

  --+Name from Row Hash|[:OneAction("name")]
  --+Description from Row Hash|[:OneAction("description")]
  --+Row ID from Row Hash|[:OneAction("_sectionid")]

  --+|[c][b]When Should I Use Each One?[/b][/c]

  --+Array|Use an array when you mainly need an ordered list and want to loop through it.
  --+Hashtable|Use a hashtable when you want to look up several fields by a meaningful key.
  --+One-Row Hashtable|Use a one-row hashtable when you already know the row ID and want several fields from that row.

  --+|[c][b]Finished[/b][/c]

  --+Result|The same repeating section was converted into arrays and hashtables without changing the character.
  --X|

  --:NoRows|
  --+|[c][b]No Action Rows Found[/b][/c]
  --+Result|Select an NPC with at least one normal Action and run the tutorial again.
}}
